From 359efe1428ef0064d4566b03f0ccecaf7e6dc667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:12:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ordered assembly by values: fixes of an independent review

- The kernel checks the row of each contribution as well as its column:
  contributions computed for a matrix with the same columns at other
  positions of the rows are detected. 32-bit integer divisions.
- The offsets of the contributions are checked to be consistent with them.
- MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator: the contributions are kept for one
  matrix of each layout of the rows and computed again before the assembly
  of another matrix, instead of after a failed attempt; contributions just
  computed which do not match the matrix are reported.
- Documentation: positions computed by a kernel, memory on the host and on
  the device, matrices alternated.
- Tests: values of the ordered assembly compared to the atomic additions
  in the three layouts of the rows, matrices of the same layout
  alternated, contributions of other rows, inconsistent offsets and
  degrees of freedom outside of the matrix detected.
